Article 145: Rules of Court, etc
Part: Part V - The Union
Clause (1): (1) Subject to the provisions of any law made 
by Parliament, the Supreme Court may from time to time, with the approval of 
the President, make rules for regulating generally the practice and procedure of 
the Court including— 
(a) rules as to the persons practising before the Court; 

